{"title":"2022 SSMO Relay Round 4 Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_4_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On each day, a robot finds a new organism with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a3588bb395f693f5fd014687a9b680837fd2dc6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, an already discovered organism with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a270a7be617f39b92e4821298c4555cffe496c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.2$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />, and nothing with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8e15844d523efe58af54649ee285b2c23a96b20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"22\" height=\"13\" />. If a new organism is found, the robot correctly identifies it as new with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/27495cbe2044b503d98fb795bb2e0adc0a197062.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.9$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />, and if a discovered organism is found, the robot correctly identifies it as discovered with probability <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/274c3ed420a60124420c39b147c9a39b6778d0f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.75$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />. The expected number of days until the robot reports that it has found a new organism can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_4_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2022 SSMO Relay Round 4 Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_4_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd3c67c6710fa378ba458c6e0556276c8f340aed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = TNYWR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"14\" />. The roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29c7a4d3bfe8d2af309c54c3ca404cf39db86cf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=x^3+5x+8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"21\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7b236356b58f659ef3b68fe9bdb6e48399210fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1,r_2,r_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/0/750f53cd0ff1b9b07337b88051e797c86c60f571.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_n(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" /> be a polynomial with roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d8012d771839d1660b0dc5a67359ab3e5e1ef756.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1+n, r_2+n,r_3+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"164\" height=\"16\" />. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd8534f6e65f3b8cac1c3618387342e45654a76a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{n=1}^{T}(-1)^{n}g_n(5),\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"51\" /> is divided by 1000.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_4_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2022 SSMO Relay Round 4 Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_4_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd3c67c6710fa378ba458c6e0556276c8f340aed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T = TNYWR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"117\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/0/ae0734db2c961f41d5627f830ea0e5c1de76262f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\mathbb{Z}\\to\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"18\" /> satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc73712d7f1001a98e82f12a2706d1004bae0610.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/8/7580cb0af473be727d28ee661c66c98a0a8f5a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/8/e5803550b5cb87d23083ccc09f35d30c5f8052ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n+2)=12f(n+1)-20f(n)\\]\" width=\"251\" height=\"18\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/9587f4255ca590d37018e5703bef62e537354e41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(T)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_SSMO_Relay_Round_4_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2022 SSMO Relay Round 4 Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018064500\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.017 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.030 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 109/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3988/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:24543:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018064500 and revision id 280196. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}